From 14407e68cc013f719ab16f9ac34af1dee5466277 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 17:38:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/12] [jakompiled] runtime: the Jak 2 engine (GAME.CGO) links
 and runs in the browser

- mips2c functions: a pool of adapters with the GOAL function type that build the MIPS
  ExecutionContext like _mips2c_call_systemv (fake GOAL stack below it, v0 as the result)
- nothing / zero-func: wasm functions instead of x86 ret stubs
- C functions with arg3_is_pp (new basic, copy basic, method-set!) get the current pp as their
  4th argument through an intermediate adapter, like the x86 trampoline
- goalc-wasm --debug-calls: check every call_indirect at runtime (env.check_call) and report
  bad function objects with the call site
